<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sawankhalok ware</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th–16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Si Satchanalai ware</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sawankhalok ware is the glazed stoneware made at the kilns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/si-satchanalai">Si Satchanalai</a>, near Sawankhalok in north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, from about the fourteenth to the sixteenth century. It includes green celadons, brown and white wares and pieces painted in iron black under the glaze. Exported widely, it has been found in shipwrecks and sites across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> and other parts of maritime <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>.</p></div>
